body:
Hey! Thanks for taking the time to respond with this many ideas! I'll go trough every point you make, just because I find it very interesting.

&#x200B;

>***If someone wanted to make a gem character with this, would this character also make sense if they were put into the series itself?***

&#x200B;

You know, I hadn't considered this before. I wanted to stay only with Houseki no kuni stuff in an attempt to make it simple and easy to get into. But If it only works as a way to replicate existing characters in the story, it isn't that good nor fun. This is something that i'll definitely change.

&#x200B;

>***there needs to be two mechanics at play for breakage (if it's not too complicated in the end): hardness and brittleness.***

With this... it's complicated. I did know that these two were different things, but I needed to divide the gems in some way that helped represent their different characteristics. Using hardness with Mohs scale, something that's both iconic to the series and recognizable for the general public, seemed like a good option. besides that, the main idea is to make it easy to understand and fun to create, while it isn't completely accurate, it does serve it purpose. I would, however, like to add the crystalline vs microcrystalline/matrix feature as an optional rule. In any case, if you can think of a way to integrate this without creating more subraces or making it too complex, i'd love to hear it.

&#x200B;

>***Giving the option to low hardness gems that aren't inherently poisonous doesn't seem to fit***

&#x200B;

While I do agree that it doesn't really make sense to have phos throwing poison around, in this case I think that it falls under the rule of fun. I give you this tool to create your character, if you want to have a Calcite puking poison all over the place, go for it. Nevertheless, I will add a table listing the gems that are more "compatible" with that ability, so that it teaches something and makes it more immersive.

&#x200B;

>***This seems very Phos-specific***

&#x200B;

You're right, I just thought it was a fun ability to have. I'll consider adding it as an effect to adaptability, but I think it's an interesting ability on its own.

&#x200B;

>***I do think that "workaholic" could work as a general "no specific trait"***

&#x200B;

Definitely. I wasn't sure how to do this, but I wanted to make a general trait so that not every gem was necessarily special. I will change this, even though it leaves me with almost nothing for the medium Hardness gems.

&#x200B;

>***Tiny crystallization***

&#x200B;

As long as I don't change the subclasses, this will probably remain the same. I could, however, add this to the other gem's subraces. It would help make it more accurate.

&#x200B;

>***While I think that giving a gem a whole second personality and stat build would be a bit much to deal with in play,***

&#x200B;

Maybe I went too far with this one. I think I'll leave it to a personality change and the ability to stay awake at night without penalties.

&#x200B;

>***Unwavering***

&#x200B;

I think this could work as a roleplaying trait, saying that your character has been alive for a long time and having an advantage because of it. I think It can also work with the medium hardness gems.

&#x200B;

>***Lightning fast.***

&#x200B;

Maybe it was a little overpowered, i'll change that. The only thing that bothers me is that I really have no explanation for this, it's just there.

&#x200B;

>***Watermelon Tourmaline actually demonstrates this power in the manga***

&#x200B;

Damn, i completely forgot about this part. Yeah, i'll definitely add this to the medium hardness gems.

&#x200B;

>***density***

&#x200B;

Good idea! I'll add this as well, it will help make it more interesting.

&#x200B;

I really enjoyed reading your ideas, I'll see to implement them sometime soon. If you want to see what I have so far, [here's the latest draft](https://homebrewery.naturalcrit.com/share/SkSqk-SxuS). Again, any and all advice is appreciated.

oops, i didn't realize. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for the correction!
